  "slug": "three-consecutive-odds",
  "title": "Three Consecutive Odds",
  "category": "dsa",
  "subcategory": "arrays",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "tags": [
    "Array"
  ],
  "statement": "Given an integer array `arr`, return `true` if there are three consecutive odd numbers in the array. Otherwise, return `false`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: arr = [2,6,4,1]\nOutput: false\nExplanation: There are no three consecutive odds.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: arr = [1,2,34,3,4,5,7,23,12]\nOutput: true\nExplanation: [5,7,23] are three consecutive odds.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= arr.length <= 1000`\n*   `1 <= arr[i] <= 1000`",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= arr.length <= 1000",
    "1 <= arr[i] <= 1000"
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "arr = [2,6,4,1]",
      "output": "false",
      "explanation": "There are no three consecutive odds."
    },
    {
      "input": "arr = [1,2,34,3,4,5,7,23,12]",
      "output": "true",
      "explanation": "[5,7,23] are three consecutive odds."
    }
  ],
